evoxd (0.7.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Layout: "HOW TO USE" is a heading on its own line above step 1; the
    steps use the full width.
  * Details button reads "OPEN DETAILS" / "CLOSE DETAILS". The details
    area never enlarges the window: it takes space from the list, its
    height follows its content, and closing it restores the window size
    (unless the user resized the window meanwhile).
  * RAM in steps of 0.25 GB (256 MiB) from 1 GB; old remembered values are
    rounded to the grid. New recommendation: peak + 25 %, rounded up to
    0.25 GB, at least 1 GB; above 85 % of the assigned RAM the hint asks
    for more RAM.

 -- EVOXsecure <341397211+EVOXsecure@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200

evoxd (0.7.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Faster live values: while a disposable VM is running, RAM, CPU and
    network are read every 1 s (memory balloon statistics period 1 s);
    without a running VM the 5 s cycle stays. Reading happens in a
    background thread; a delayed reading is skipped, errors never disturb.
  * Large details area behind a prominent "DETAILS" button directly under
    the list (about half the window height). Opens automatically when a
    running VM is selected unless closed explicitly; the choice is
    remembered. Bigger numbers and thicker bars.

 -- EVOXsecure <341397211+EVOXsecure@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0200

evoxd (0.7.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Real RAM use: the virtio memory balloon now reports guest memory
    statistics every 5 s (read-only from the host via libvirt; no new
    guest-host channel). Without guest figures "n/a" or an estimate marked
    "~"; never invented values.
  * DISPOSABLE list is slimmer: name, state, mode, running time, compact RAM
    traffic light, CPU percent.
  * Details area with three blocks: RAM bar with zones (green up to 60 %,
    yellow up to 85 %, red above) and peak mark with time; CPU bar with a
    short history; network/overlay with fill level, template, mode, network
    lock state and start count of the purpose. Folded state is remembered.
  * Stop and erase shows a one-line RAM hint (information only) with an
    opt-in "Remember ... for <purpose>" button.
  * Start dialog shows the highest RAM use of the purpose so far (hint only).
  * HOW-TO step 4 glow uses the button colour (purple / blue).

