evoxd (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Live values per running disposable VM (read-only from libvirt statistics):
    RAM traffic light with symbol and word (OK / HIGH / FULL / LOW) and peak,
    CPU percent, running time, network traffic, overlay size. Shown in the
    details bar and as compact columns in the DISPOSABLE list; "n/a" when a
    value is not available. Updated only in the existing 5 s cycle and only
    when the display really changes.
  * Fix: rare "ValueError: seek of closed file" from the VM window check
    (the check could run twice; now exactly once, timer removed, file closed
    when the window closes).
  * Start dialog: optional "Remember RAM for <purpose>" (off by default),
    stored in ~/.config/evoxd/config.json; only the RAM size, still limited
    by free memory. Mode and network lock are never remembered.

