    version and size; option "all older versions, keep the newest"). Only
    copies in the pool evoxd-templates with registry entry and expected
    path; never the original domain, never VAULT-*. Refused while any VM
    uses the copy as backing file (registry and libvirt). Version numbers
    are never reused.
  * Damaged copies: a checksum mismatch marks the copy DAMAGED; no new VMs
    start from it until it is imported again or removed. Registry schema 2.
  * GUI setting "Verify template after each VM shutdown" (default off,
    stored in ~/.config/evoxd/config.json): background check after stop,
    destroy or guest shutdown; result in the status line, red on mismatch.
  * GUI: templates named *-BACKUP shown in red (selection, list, import
    dialog); import dialog starts without a preselected row; template area
    larger and growing with the window; window size remembered; signal
    colours readable on light and dark themes; uniform spacing; own icon.
  * "evoxd template-verify NAME --version N"; template-list shows size and
    DAMAGED.

