evoxd (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Memory check: uses MemAvailable, VM RAM plus 256 MiB overhead and a
    configurable host reserve (~/.config/evoxd/config.json, host_reserve_mib,
    default 2 GiB). Warning only if less than the reserve stays available,
    start refused below half the reserve. Same check in GUI and CLI.
  * GUI: start dialog shows host memory, reserve, room for VMs and max. CPUs;
    RAM and CPU input limited to these maxima.
  * GUI: "Open console" renamed to "Show selected VM"; errors of the VM
    window (virt-viewer) are shown in the status line.
  * GUI and "evoxd list": RAM and CPUs per VM, read from the domain XML.
  * GUI: all texts in one module, groups Host / VM list / buttons + status
    line, network lock shown green (active) or red (problem).

